    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Description\n\nI frequently use visual mode to simulate a contiguous multi cursor to insert the same thing on many lines.  Very often this is to surround a token in multiple similar statements with e.g. `\"` or `'`.  In this scenario I don't want mini.pairs to insert a matching pair.  I got this working creating a `ModeChanged` autocmd in my lazy config and it struck me that this might be useful for others - maybe it could be incorporated into the plugin?  Here's my lazy.vim plugin spec with the code:\n\n```lua\n  return   {\n    'echasnovski/mini.pairs',\n    version = '*',\n    event = \"VeryLazy\",\n    opts = {\n      modes = { insert = true, command = false, terminal = false },\n      -- skip autopair when next character is one of these\n      skip_next = [=[[%w%%%'%[%\"%.%`%$]]=],\n      -- skip autopair when the cursor is inside these treesitter nodes\n      skip_ts = { \"string\" },\n      -- skip autopair when next character is closing pair\n      -- and there are more closing pairs than opening pairs\n      skip_unbalanced = true,\n      -- better deal with markdown code blocks\n      markdown = true,\n    },\n    config = function(PluginSpec, opts)\n      require('mini.pairs').setup(opts)\n      vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"ModeChanged\", {\n        group = \"MiniPairs\", -- same as the group in `mini.pairs`\n        pattern = \"*:*\",\n        callback = function()\n          if (vim.v.event.old_mode == \"\\22\" or vim.v.event.old_mode == \"V\") and vim.v.event.new_mode == \"i\"  then\n            vim.b.visual_insert = true\n            vim.b.minipairs_disable = true\n          elseif vim.b.visual_insert == true then\n            vim.b.minipairs_disable = false\n            vim.b.visual_insert = false\n          end\n        end\n      })\n    end,\n  },\n```",
